      "path": "/books/al-kafi:5:2:93:6",
      "text": [
        " شِرَاءِ الرُّومِيَّاتِ قَالَ اشْتَرِهِنَّ وَ بِعْهُنَّ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Ismail, from Al Fazl Bin Shazaan, from Ibn Abu Umeyr, from Ibrahim Bin Abdul Hameed, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Al-Hassan<sup>asws</sup> regarding the Roman women (slaves). He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘Buy them and sell them’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "6. Muhammad ibn ‘Isma’il has narrated from al-Fadl ibn Shadhan from ibn abu ‘Umayr from fbrahim ibn ‘Abd al-Hamid who has said the foiiowing: “About the case of buying and the sale of Romans, abu al-Hassan, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘(If they are for sale), buy and sell them.’” "
        ]
      }
